What is NOT licensed here
-------------------------

The underlying ENTRIES are not ours to relicense. Each record describes software
published by a national, municipal or international catalogue under that
catalogue's own terms, and those terms differ — some are explicitly open, some
are unstated, some are public-sector-information regimes specific to one country.

Every entry carries `source` and, where one exists, `entry_url` — a deep link
back to the record upstream. `sources.py` (published as /sources.json) lists all
17 catalogues with their access routes. Check the upstream terms before
redistributing entry content at scale; do not assume this file grants them.

Cached raw checkpoints under `cache/` are verbatim upstream responses, retained
so the pipeline can be replayed offline without hitting other people's
infrastructure. They are upstream's data in upstream's shape, not ours.

Nothing here licenses the CATALOGUED SOFTWARE itself. Each project's own licence
governs its use; `licence_spdx` records it where the upstream string is real SPDX
and is null rather than guessed where it is not.


